\ port/gforth/boot.4 - relfsh's boot word on gforth: loaded after the
\ shell's sources; build.sh saves the image (gforthmi: relocatable).

BASE @  DECIMAL

\ gforth catches nearly every signal itself, to THROW or to exit; relf's
\ engine leaves them as the process found them. Back to the default, all
\ but the faults - gforth's THROW for those is relf's own trap route.
: SIGNALS-DEFAULT ( --- )
  32 1 DO
    I 4 = I 5 = OR I 7 = OR I 8 = OR I 11 = OR I 9 = OR I 19 = OR 0= IF
      I 0 SIG-DISPOSE DROP
    THEN
  LOOP ;

' 'cold DEFER@ CONSTANT GFORTH-COLD     \ gforth's own start-up hooks, run first
: PORT-BOOT ( --- )
  GFORTH-COLD EXECUTE  RELFSYS-OPEN       \ sys.fs's library, opened again
  ONLY FORTH  RELF-WORDLIST >order  RELF-WORDLIST set-current   \ kernel.4's
  0 ENV-V !  0 SIG-CAUGHT !  0 SIG-SEEN !  -1 SIG-FD !  LSAVE-INIT
  0 TIO-SAVED? !  -1 RAW-FD !
  DSTACK-INIT  SIGNALS-DEFAULT  ARGV0-DEFAULT
  MAIN ;
' PORT-BOOT IS 'cold

BASE !
